            <ArticleTitle>Low-molecular-weight heparin-associated fat necrosis of the breast.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>193-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fat necrosis of the breast is a well-recognised complication of unfractionated heparin. The following is a case of fat necrosis due to low-molecular-weight heparin in a 91-year-old woman admitted to hospital with unstable angina.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
